{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1543333-time-purview","id":1543333,"title":"Time Purview","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-10-08T06:38:33-07:00","id":1543333,"title":"Time Purview","content":"Time is the differentations of the past, present and future, of the changing of things. Gods of this purview are present between every tick and tock<br /> <br /> Innate Power: You have an innate sense of time, knowing always the exact day,hour,month...everything!!! By rolling Intellect+Legend, you can perceive changes to the timeline<br /> <br /> -----------------------------<br /> Time Slipper<br /> Cost: Spent 1 Legend<br /> Duration: Scene<br /> Subject: Self<br /> Action: Simple<br /> <br /> You can exit in time during a scene, then return to same location in the next scene<br /> ------------------------<br /> Loop<br /> Cost: Imbue 2 Legend<br /> Duration: Scene<br /> Subject: All Characters<br /> Action: Complex<br /> <br /> Your character can chose a scene to repeat 1 time. It can be re used multiple times on the same scene, but it must always pay the cost of Legend<br /> ----------------------<br /> Casual Miracles<br /> -Block a scene<br /> -Put development in stasis<br /> -Put someone out of sync with the world<br /> <br /> Success<br /> <br /> Everything moves as it should and time around you move slower or faster, according to what you need.<br /> <br /> Mortal Failure<br /> <br /> Your attacks and those of your allies are never on time and sometime attack before they were cast, people age in an uncontrolled manner<br /> <br /> Basic Stunts<br /> <br /> -Advance the training(3s): For a scene all attributes get a +2<br /> <br /> -Reverse Time(1s): You turn time back of a number of scenes equal to your Resolve<br /> <br /> Entropy Acceleration(2s): You apply Damage equal to Legend * Might<br /> <br /> ---------<br /> This was my idea for a Time Purview in 2e. I'm working on an Arete one like in 1e for the Greek Pantheon<br /> <br /> EDIT: Yeah the way the Legend was used for the boons was not clear","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28580,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28580-madoglio14","user":"Madoglio14","date":". 02-22-2025, 06:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28580-madoglio14","name":"Madoglio14","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"26"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-08T07:27:25-07:00","id":1543336,"title":"","content":"The Stars purview covered time. To have a Time Purview you'd also have to make a new Stars Purview.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-08T08:55:50-07:00","id":1543341,"title":"","content":"Well, the actual Stars boon effects don't really overlap that much with what's here. I'd say you could just leave Stars as is and still have Time as a separate (or possibly specialised?) purview.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26730-tomdick-harry","name":"TomDick&Harry","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-08T12:51:50-07:00","id":1543356,"title":"","content":"I just read the Star purview and only one boon, and that was because the stars are so ancient to have seen the past , even in the Demigod book part of Dominion there it wasn't really explicit about Time, but of the role of the stars and the firmament. Maybe i read something wrong, let me know. On a sidenote, do you think mechanically is too broken ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28580-madoglio14","name":"Madoglio14","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"26"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-08T20:21:00-07:00","id":1543384,"title":"","content":"Time's kind of divided between Epic Dexterity and Stars in terms of Purviews, with Epic Dexterity focusing on the speed aspect of it and Stars more the divination (though it DOES also have a speed-adjusting effect with the Mythos). Still, it looks pretty interesting to me, though I'm wondering about whether the Legend cost is Imbued or Spent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26317-critian-caceorte","name":"Critian Caceorte","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-09T03:31:08-07:00","id":1543408,"title":"","content":"I was thinking spent","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28580-madoglio14","name":"Madoglio14","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"26"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}